---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Work"
  description="Work with John Crenshaw — deciding what to build, what to leave alone, and where AI actually belongs."
  windowTitle="Work"
  active="work"
>
  <div class="room-head">
    <h1 class="room-title">Work with me</h1>
    <p class="room-lead">The right tool for the job, and telling you when you don't need one.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      For a career I built other people's systems under other people's constraints, regulated
      and high-stakes: HIPAA subrogation by the thousands of cases a day, a Y2K trading-system
      conversion that physically could not slip, a decade moving SMS at platform scale inside
      Salesforce. I could always see what I'd have done differently, and it was never my call.
      Now it is.
    </p>
    <p>
      This is the part I'm actually good at: helping you decide what to build, what to leave
      alone, and where AI earns its place and where it doesn't. Sometimes that's custom software,
      built properly and handed over clean. Often it's less than you walked in expecting, and I'll
      tell you so even when it costs me the work. The honest answer is the product.
    </p>
    <p>
      If that's the conversation you want,
      <a href="mailto:work@jcrenshaw.dev?subject=Working%20together">send a note</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
